#MISE description="Run the warrant unit tests — service and request client (no network, no cluster)"
"""Unit tests for the approval path: `containers/warrant/app/main.py` and the
`mise-tasks/request-run` client that files against it.

Pure-function coverage of the parts where being wrong is an audit-integrity
problem rather than an outage — run attribution and SHA binding above all.
Needs nothing privileged: no forge token, no cluster, no vault, so it works
from an agent pod as well as from gilbert.

Two suites, deliberately in different places: the service's own tests live
inside its build context (`containers/warrant/tests/`), while tests for repo
tooling live in `tests/` so nothing reaches up out of a container directory.

The dependency pins here mirror what nixpkgs supplies to the image (see
`containers/warrant/default.nix`); they are close enough for unit tests, and
divergence in a *major* version is a signal worth chasing, not noise.

Usage: mise run warrant-test [-- <pytest args>]
"""

import pathlib
import sys

import pytest

ROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
SUITES = [ROOT / "containers" / "warrant" / "tests", ROOT / "tests"]

sys.exit(pytest.main([*map(str, SUITES), "-q", *sys.argv[1:]]))
